// The one retired spelling the package still reads, in order to refuse it
// with the text to write. This file is no part of the language: `stage.lark`
// is the language, and `syntax.parse.parse_text` reads a text with these
// rules only after the language's own parser has refused it.
//
// A bound written after a comma, γ : ℝ₊, < 2, is a spelling AMD-GRAM-004
// retired; the same bound is now an interval written after @,
// γ : ℝ₊ @ (-inf, 2). The lowering refuses a declaration that carries one
// and gives the sets to write (`syntax.lower._retired_bound_refusal`).
%extend declaration: subject_path typing declared_value? retired_bound STMT_META?
    | tuple_subject typing? declared_value? retired_bound STMT_META?
retired_bound: ("," RELOP formula)+
